If a patient receives a methadone-treatment for an opioid-use-disorder and requires an additional-opioid for a severe-acute-pain then every clinician should carefully monitor the patient.
If a patient receives a methadone-treatment for an opioid-use-disorder and requires an additional-opioid for a severe-acute-pain and a pain-care-clinician-treatment is feasible then the patient should optimally receive the pain-care-clinician-treatment with an opioid-treatment-program-consultation.
